	doi = {10/gk5bfq},
	abstract = {This paper describes socio-material practices of digital nomads who live locationindependent and work online. Their business models are based on data-driven platforms. Optimizing oneself as an individual is understood as a key element of a digital capitalist logic. Based on an empirical study, the paper outlines digital capitalism as co-produced by individuals who do no longer understand themselves as citizens of specific states. Its main ideas can be traced back to the beginning of the development of the World Wide Web and what is called “new economy”.},
